
A. THE LIVE READING — HELD AFTER THE CONFIRMATION, RELEASED BY THE PERSON
  [PASS] A1. the confirmation has been spoken and the person has not answered: FINAL_YES is read but the closing response is awaited
  [PASS] A2. the registration is read as confirmed from the person's yes, before the agent has replied
  [PASS] A3. the person's closing word, answered by the goodbye, releases the hangup
  [PASS] A4. ...and while the goodbye is still being spoken nothing fires
  [PASS] A5. the AGENT cannot release the hold on the person's behalf
  [PASS] A6. a question after the confirmation is held by the EXISTING guard, and the person's closing then releases it
  [PASS] A7. a retraction after the confirmation still flips the verdict — nothing about the classifier moved
  [PASS] A8. every non-registration ending is untouched: FINAL_NO, undecided, empty
  [PASS] A10. `closingDelivered`: true only when the agent's LATEST turn is a delivered sign-off
  [PASS] A9. the hangup and the sheet still cannot disagree

B. THE CLOSING VOCABULARY BOUNDARY
  [PASS] B1. a bare closing pleasantry is recognised, in English, Hinglish and Devanagari
  [PASS] B2. anything with content of its own is NOT a closing — it belongs to the language model
  [PASS] B3. no negation is ever a closing — a refusal or a retraction must reach the model
  [PASS] B4. a long sentence is not a pleasantry, and a question mark is disqualifying

C. THE PIPELINE — ONE FIXED GOODBYE, WITHOUT THE LANGUAGE MODEL
